                <pb facs="0897" n="799" sameAs="frus:frus1900/pg799"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Newel to Mr. Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The
                                Hague</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1900-10-13"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">October 13,
                    1900</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>[Mr. Newel reports that, in company with the Russian minister, he called at noon
                    to-day on Mr. Asser, who very cordially consents to act as arbitrator if
                    appointed. Mr. Asser would prefer to leave the compensation to be determined by
                    parties to the convention.]</p>
            </div>
